Subject: kernel: qualcommbe: CMA for DT reserved pools

Contiguous memory allocator without a default global pool
(CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=0): only shared-dma-pool regions from the device tree use
it. Needed to hand the ath12k dual-MAC firmware its MLO global memory only
while the 5 GHz split is on, instead of keeping 12 MB no-map all the time.
Batched into 1.4.0 so the kernel config hash does not move again in 1.4.x.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/config-6.18
@@ -646,3 +646,14 @@
 CONFIG_ZSTD_COMMON=y
 CONFIG_ZSTD_COMPRESS=y
 CONFIG_ZSTD_DECOMPRESS=y
+CONFIG_CMA=y
+CONFIG_CMA_ALIGNMENT=8
+CONFIG_CMA_AREAS=8
+# CONFIG_CMA_DEBUGFS is not set
+CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=0
+CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_SEL_MBYTES=y
+# CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_SEL_MAX is not set
+# CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_SEL_MIN is not set
+# CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_SEL_PERCENTAGE is not set
+# CONFIG_CMA_SYSFS is not set
+CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
